# TraceIQ — local configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every value here has a working default, so `docker compose up` needs no `.env` at all. Copy this file only
# to change something.
#
# These are the same variables the API and the CLI already read; nothing is invented for the container.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chat
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which model answers. **Empty by default, and that is deliberate.**
#
# A model is several gigabytes, and a first `docker compose up` should not open with a download nobody asked
# for. Left empty, everything except chat works: the API starts, reports `chat disabled`, and answers
# `503 ai-not-configured` on the two chat endpoints, which the web UI renders as a clear message.
#
# Set it and run `docker compose up` again to enable chat. The pull happens once, into a persistent volume,
# and the API waits for it to finish before starting.
#
# Verified against: qwen2.5:7b-instruct (~4.7 GB, a 32k context window).
TRACEIQ_MODEL=

# How much context the model is actually run with. Optional; 16384 by default.
#
# **This is the number the prompt is budgeted against, and it must be the number the daemon uses.** The
# model reports the context it was *trained* with — 32768 for the model above — but with no explicit
# setting the daemon picks its own, changes it between requests, and silently discards the front of an
# over-long prompt. Measured before this was fixed: a 6,043-token prompt came back with
# prompt_eval_count 2050, and what had been cut was the system prompt and the highest-priority facts.
#
# TraceIQ now sends this value as num_ctx on every request, so the two cannot disagree. The window used
# is min(this, what the model was trained with), so raising it never asks a small model for more than
# it has.
#
# Raising it costs memory for the key/value cache and, because the fact budget follows it, time: prompt
# evaluation on a 7B CPU container was measured at 45.75 tokens per second, so every extra 1,000 tokens
# of prompt is another 22 seconds before the first word appears. A GPU deployment should raise it.
TRACEIQ_MODEL_CONTEXT=16384

# Which provider holds it. `ollama` is the only one implemented; the value exists because the AI layer is
# provider-agnostic and the CLI takes the same flag.
TRACEIQ_PROVIDER=ollama

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to analyse
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The repository TraceIQ scans, as a path **on the host**. Mounted read-only into the API container, which is
# what performs the scan.
#
# Defaults to this checkout — so out of the box TraceIQ analyses itself, which is the quickest way to see what
# it does. Point it at any repository, in any language: TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Java and Go are parsed
# semantically, and everything else is described by its files, manifests, dependencies and artefacts.
TRACEIQ_SCAN_PATH=.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ports, all bound to localhost
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The web application. This is the one to open.
WEB_PORT=3001

# The REST API. Useful directly: curl http://localhost:3000/overview
API_PORT=3000

# The model provider. Exposed so `ollama` on the host can talk to the same models.
OLLAMA_PORT=11434

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Advanced
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the browser's /api/* calls are forwarded.
#
# **This is a build-time value.** Next compiles its rewrites into the build, so changing it requires
# rebuilding the web image (`docker compose build web`) — setting it on a running container has no effect.
# The default is the Compose service name and is correct for this stack; change it only when running the web
# image against an API somewhere else.
TRACEIQ_API_URL=http://api:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository Analysis
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where cloned repositories are written before they are scanned.
#
# Defaults to the system temporary directory. Each analysis gets its own directory beneath it and removes
# it afterwards, whether the analysis succeeded or not. Set this to put clones on a larger or faster disk.
TRACEIQ_WORKSPACE_ROOT=

# How long a clone may take, in milliseconds. Default 600000 (ten minutes).
#
# A large repository on a slow link can exceed this; the analysis then fails with `analysis-timeout`
# rather than hanging.
TRACEIQ_CLONE_TIMEOUT_MS=

# The largest repository that may be cloned, in megabytes. Default 2048.
#
# The clone is watched as it grows and killed if it crosses this, so a very large repository fails with
# `repository-too-large` instead of filling the disk.
TRACEIQ_MAX_CLONE_MB=
